# FRIDAY MODE: confident_explore
#
# THE FROZEN PARAMETERS OF THE BEST RUN SHE HAS EVER DONE — 2026-09-04 21:18,
# twenty minutes, and the configuration Harsh asked to keep permanently:
#
#   "This run was THE BEST ONE YET... Whenever I ask you to run her again she
#    should be able to run it like it did in the last run without any
#    hesitation, stutter and full confidence."
#
# Measured against the two preceding full-length runs:
#
#                          16:09     17:21     21:18
#     loop median         138.6 ms    48.7     34.3 ms
#     over 100 ms budget      62%      30%        13%
#     ToF reflex firing       85%      75%        44%
#     ground driven        20.9 m     41.7     59.2 m
#     time driving             8%      16%        26%
#     time spinning in place  n/a      35%        21%
#     map               discarded    kept    299.6 m^2
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH FOR THOSE FLAGS. Nothing else should
# hard-code them: modes/explore.sh reads this, and the systemd unit runs that,
# so there is exactly one place where "how she runs" is written down.
#
# The code half of the configuration is the git tag `run-20260904-2118-best`.
# Flags alone will not reproduce the run if rl/ has moved on; restore both:
#
#     git checkout run-20260904-2118-best -- rl/
#
# RESTORED 2026-09-17. Harsh: "when i was building llm driven some things got
# mismatched and same spinning behaviour came ... i want this run behaviour back
# and also will be triggered by dashboard same this run". Everything added to
# the driving code after the tag (near_memory, decisive/reverse escape, brain
# targeting, the 09-12 demo ToF 0.12/0.14 stop line and 8.0 rad/s^2 slew) is
# gone from the run: pi_deploy.py, navigator.py, dwa.py and
# friday_localnav_deploy.py are BYTE-IDENTICAL to the tag again. The ACT policy
# (friday_localnav_act.onnx, 09-02 19:04) was never changed.
#
# What is NOT the tag, each for a reason written at its flag below:
#   - the LiDAR self-mask, because the ROBOT changed after 21:18
#   - the dashboard stays up and friday-mcp keeps running on the hardware
#     lease, because the dashboard is what starts and stops the run now
#   - the cameras are off, because they steer nothing and cost the loop time
#
# ⚠ THE TAG'S PARSER DOES NOT KNOW --brain-target, --no-reverse-escape,
# --no-decisive-escape OR --no-near-memory. Passing any of them aborts the run
# before she moves, so MODE_BRAIN_TARGET and MODE_REVERSE_ESCAPE below must keep
# the values that pass nothing.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Wheels live. --i-am-watching is the deliberate speed bump on autonomous
# driving and it is passed here because a MODE is, by definition, the case
# where a human has already decided.
MODE_MOTOR="friday"

# How fast she may drive on an arc she has SIMULATED CLEAR against the live scan.
# Without any authority she is only ever as decisive as the policy, and this
# policy is timid (measured mean v_raw +0.206 m/s; it asks for 0.026 in an open
# room), which is the difference between exploring and creeping.
#
# 0.6 -> 0.5 on 2026-09-05. Harsh: "just decrease the motors speed a little it
# will increase gear motors life and little jerkyness to the body only". This is
# 0.30 -> 0.25 m/s in the driving regime: about 17% slower, proportionally less
# current through the gearboxes, and smaller velocity steps for the slew limiter
# to work through, which is where the jerk comes from.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE RIGHT KNOB FOR "SLOWER". THE MOTOR DUTY CEILING IS NOT.
# The obvious alternative -- dropping --motor-max-duty below 0.85 -- BREAKS
# REVERSE, because the stiction floor is min_duty/(255*max_duty)*wheel_speed_max
# and it moves the WRONG WAY when the ceiling comes down:
#
#     max_duty 0.85 -> floor 0.1487 m/s   reverse (v_min -0.15) still executable
#     max_duty 0.80 -> floor 0.1580 m/s   EVERY reverse is now under the floor
#     max_duty 0.75 -> floor 0.1686 m/s   ...and executes as a stop
#
# The boundary is 0.8429, so 0.85 has 0.001 m/s of margin and nothing to give.
# Below it every reverse becomes an unexecutable command, the capability adapter
# substitutes a pivot, and she is back to spinning in place instead of backing
# out -- which is exactly the failure fixed on 2026-09-04. Leave the ceiling
# alone; slow her down here.
# RESTORED TO 0.6, which is what the 21:18 run -- the one this mode was saved
# FROM -- actually used. e6ba7f9 lowered it to 0.5 as "a gentler exploration
# speed" on 2026-09-05, and that is the "steering speed decreased" Harsh
# reported on 2026-09-06. He asked for the old run back, permanently.
MODE_NAV_AUTHORITY="0.6"

# Twenty minutes. Long enough for the map to grow and for the frontier planner
# to finish targets it starts; short enough to watch.
MODE_DURATION="1200"

# She narrates. For a demo this is most of the effect, and the narration runs
# on its own thread and cannot delay the control loop.
MODE_VOICE="1"

# WHICH OF FRIDAY'S SERVICES ARE STOPPED WHILE SHE DRIVES.
#
# HISTORY, because the measurements below are still the reason the face goes
# down and must not be read as describing the current setting: this was
# face + brain + dashboard, which is what the 21:18 run used. It is now the
# face alone -- see the 2026-09-08 note at the bottom of this section.
#
# Measured, same robot, same navigation code, with ALL THREE stopped:
#
#     services stopped (the good run)   loop  77 ms   reflex 30%   ~515 deg/m
#     services up      (2026-09-06)     loop 203 ms   reflex 59%    569 deg/m
#                                       90% of ticks over the 100 ms deadline
#
# run_localnav.sh explains what that costs: "A 0.55 rad/s bias held for 266 ms
# instead of 100 is a 2.7x oversteer -- she swings past the heading, the next
# tick corrects, and that overshoot-correct cycle is the ZIG-ZAG Harsh
# watched."
#
# THIS REVERSES HARSH'S 2026-09-05 REQUEST ("all the mcp tools dashboard face
# and everything will continuously work while exploring") AND THAT IS
# DELIBERATE. Harsh, 2026-09-06, after seeing both black boxes side by side:
# "do all the three fixes and pls make it permanent because i dont want to
# change because i love the old run". Navigation quality won over the demo.
#
# She still TALKS during the run -- MODE_VOICE=1 below is pi_deploy's own
# voice and does not go through the MCP server, so it survives the quiet.
# Set to 0 for a demo where the face matters more than the driving.
# Harsh, 2026-09-08: "just like dont stop just the face and keep the dashboard
# alive during the run as well as add the stop button in dashboard and
# everything stops its okay".
#
# ONLY THE FACE IS STOPPED NOW. The face is the one that measurably costs a
# core (84.5% standing still); friday-brain was the other expensive one until
# the lock convoy in stt.Subscription.frames() was fixed, which gave a whole
# core back, and friday-dashboard is ~2% idle. The dashboard has to stay up for
# a different reason than CPU: THE STOP BUTTON IS IN IT, and a run that stops
# the dashboard is a run nobody can stop from the phone.
#
# ⚠ THE COST IS CAMERAS, NOT CPU. friday-dashboard's ffmpeg children hold BOTH
# /dev/video nodes while anyone has its camera panel open, and a V4L2 device
# does not survive two streaming readers -- measured 2026-09-04, with the panel
# open both cameras returned ZERO frames to the robot. run_localnav.sh warns
# when something already holds a camera; a camera-blind run looks exactly like
# a working one in the log, so read that warning. CLOSE THE CAMERA PANEL BEFORE
# A RUN.
#
# MODE_QUIET_SERVICES="1" is the old behaviour (face + brain + dashboard) and
# is what the 21:18 measurements were taken with.
# HARSH, 2026-09-12 (judging): "all the services including offline.py and rl
# exploration model will be alive during the run ... after finishing all the
# services comes up". EMPTY = STOP NOTHING. The face stays up too now, so the
# panel is alive in front of the judges. run_localnav.sh restores whatever it
# stopped via `trap restore_units EXIT INT TERM`, so an empty list simply means
# there is nothing to restore. COST: the face is ~84.5% of a core (measured),
# so the control loop has less CPU than the frozen 21:18 measurements had.
# Put "friday-face.service" back here to restore that configuration exactly.
#
# 2026-09-17, BACK TO A QUIET PI FOR THE RESTORED RUN: face AND brain stop,
# the dashboard stays (its stop button), and both come back when she parks.
# The 21:18 loop ran at 34 ms with nothing else on the cores; the 09-12 runs
# with everything up ran at 116 ms, and a late tick is an oversteer. The brain
# costs nothing she needs here: the wake word is hushed for the whole run
# anyway, and MODE_VOICE is pi_deploy's own voice.
#
# 2026-10-02, HARSH (File 21, after the first real mission): KEEP THE BRAIN UP.
# The exploration mission asks "what should I call this area?" while the run
# HOLDS her still, and the answer is heard by friday-brain (the mic's one
# owner) -- with the brain stopped nothing could hear him and every room was
# saved unnamed. While she drives the wake word is still hushed (main.py's
# _explore_hush), so the brain is not scoring audio then; it listens only
# while she is held. Measured idle with the wake word LISTENING: 53% of a
# core; hushed is far less. MEASURE the next run's tick time against the 09-17
# 34 ms and put friday-brain.service back here if the loop slows.
MODE_QUIET_UNITS="friday-face.service"

# BACK OUT INSTEAD OF SPINNING. Harsh, 2026-09-06: "when tof like robots front
# gets obstacles it detects but dosent like move it sticks and confuses and also
# in strict corners pls like it reacts quickly and avoid it while there is space
# by reversing".
#
# Measured in the 01:59 run, 783 REFLEX_STOP ticks:
#     frozen  (v=0, w=0)      25%
#     pivoting(v=0, w!=0)     50%   <- the "confused" spinning
#     REVERSING               24%
# and the rear gate refused a reverse 11 times in the whole run. The space was
# there; she was not using it. Longest stuck stretch ~665 ticks, about a minute.
#
# Stage 2b-bis in pi_deploy.py. It only ASKS to reverse -- stage 2d re-applies
# the rear gate to whatever any stage authored, so a reverse into a blocked rear
# is still raised to 0.0 and she pivots exactly as before. Bounded to 2 s, then
# the pivot escape and recovery take their turn.
#
# Set to 0 to get the pivot-only behaviour back, no code change.
#
# ⚠ 2026-09-17: THE RESTORED TAG HAS NO REVERSE ESCAPE AND NO SUCH FLAG. Keep
# this at 1, which passes nothing; 0 passes --no-reverse-escape and the tag's
# parser aborts the run.
MODE_REVERSE_ESCAPE="1"

# BRAIN-GUIDED TARGETING. Harsh asked for this on 2026-09-12.
#
# The brain reads what the run's own detector sees, names ONE thing to drive at,
# and writes it to state/rl_command.json; the run nudges toward it. The frontier
# planner keeps its thread and keeps choosing frontiers, so the moment the target
# goes quiet she carries on with no gap -- this adds a bias, it does not replace
# the planner.
#
# ⚠ IT IS INERT WITHOUT THE BRAIN. The writer half is main.py's
# _explore_targeter, which runs inside friday-brain.service and needs
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. With no key nothing is ever written to rl_command.json, the
# run reads an empty command forever, and the flag costs one stat() every
# TARGET_POLL_TICKS. That is the state this was turned on in.
#
# ⚠ THE BRAIN MUST STAY UP FOR THE RUN. MODE_QUIET_UNITS above stops the FACE
# only; if friday-brain is ever added back to that list, this goes dead with it.
#
# ⚠ NEVER PROVEN ON THE ROBOT. Every part is tested without one
# (scripts/test_brain_target.py) and the seam is deliberately narrow, but the
# brain -> rl_command.json -> TargetedPlanner -> wheels path has never run
# end to end with a live brain. The first run with this on is that test.
# Set to "0" to put the mode back to the frozen 21:18 configuration exactly.
#
# 0 SINCE 2026-09-17, and it must stay 0: the restored tag has no brain
# targeting, and --brain-target aborts its parser.
MODE_BRAIN_TARGET="0"


# CAMERAS OFF. Harsh, 2026-09-12, presenting to a judge: "still spinning half of
# the time ... its confused not moving forward again".
#
# The ToF phantom-cliff fix the same day took the spinning from 48-56% to ~40% and
# translating from 26% to 52% (see the sunlight note in pi_deploy.py). What was left
# is OVERSTEER, and overstreer here is a CPU problem, not a tuning one:
#
#     best run, 2026-09-04 21:18    loop p50  34 ms   13% over the 100 ms budget
#     this run, 2026-09-12 13:56    loop p50 116 ms   p90 318 ms, max 807
#
# run_localnav.sh states the cost: a 0.55 rad/s bias held for 300 ms instead of 100
# is a 3x oversteer -- she swings past the heading, the next tick corrects, and that
# overshoot-correct cycle IS the confused spinning Harsh is watching.
#
# Measured with `top -H` on the live run: the two camera threads were burning ~50%
# of a core EACH, about 180% of the process's 244% total. Stopping friday-brain
# first changed nothing (p50 100 -> 116), so the cameras are where the time is.
#
# They are advisory and they steer nothing -- `visual` contributed 0.00 on all 300
# ticks of the first instrumented run, and the safety chain is LiDAR + ToF. The
# VisualGate can only ever REDUCE authority, so losing it cannot make her less safe;
# it only removes a second opinion that was not being consulted.
#
# Set to 1 to put the cameras back.
#
# KEPT OFF for the 2026-09-17 restore, deliberately not the tag's cameras-on.
# The down camera was not delivering at 480M until 2026-09-08, so the 21:18 run
# paid for less camera than a cameras-on run does today; off is the closer
# match to the loop time that run had, and the tag's own --no-cameras does it.
MODE_CAMERAS="0"

# THE ONE HARDWARE CORRECTION, and the tag cannot run on today's robot without
# it. The tag's default mask is 88:99, measured when that was the only part of
# her body the LiDAR could see. Since then 221:237 and 319:334 (chassis,
# 2026-09-12) and 71:79 (a dome post, 2026-09-13) were measured: unmasked, four
# beams sit permanently at the 0.22 m floor, the governor vetoes forward travel
# and leaves rotation free, and she PIVOTS ON THE SPOT WITH A CLEAR PATH AHEAD --
# the spinning this restore exists to remove. Same value as HEAD's default and
# config.LIDAR_SELF_MASK. --lidar-self-mask is a tag flag, so no code changes.
# 2026-10-10: 88:99 -> 88:100. The chassis edge now returns 222-238 mm at
# raw 99 on 4 of 10 still sweeps (raw 100-103: the wall, 2.5 m, 10/10), and
# both of last night's runs sat at lidar_min 0.22-0.23 for 60-75% of ticks
# (49% on 10-07, 22% on 10-04 16:19) -- the governor braking for her own body.
MODE_LIDAR_SELF_MASK="71:79,88:100,221:237,319:334"

# --- 2026-10-02: the ACTIVE exploration back (Harsh) -------------------------
# "she is moving in short busts and very slow movement bring back the active
# exploration ... she didnt stop and reverse while she was blocked". Measured
# over the run logs: the active runs (09-19, 09-20, 09-23) drove 0.24-0.27 m/s
# forward with ~10-26 reverses a minute; since 09-28/29 0.17-0.20 m/s, 5-18 a
# minute, and 16% of ticks in the pulsed creep range on 10-02 (7-9% before).
# The two changes in between, both switchable (explore.sh):
#   a58b9e3 quieter gears (his 09-28 noise complaint) -> MODE_QUIET_MOTORS=0
#   200769c unstick (undo one move, "please move me") -> MODE_UNSTICK=0
# He chose both back to the old behaviour, friday-brain stays up. Put 1 back
# to return to the 09-29 configuration.
# 2026-10-04 (Harsh: "they make noise more than movement ... very harsh
# movements, it should be smooth"): QUIET DRIVE BACK ON. The "short bursts,
# very slow" that made him drop it on 10-02 was the 31 kHz firmware (weak
# motors), re-flashed to 490 Hz that night; on strong motors the old drive's
# kick-on-every-start is the harshness. Replayed tests #4/#5/15:43 through both
# drives: powered reversals (the clunk) 48 -> 0, kicks 138 -> 82, one-tick
# bursts 36 -> 22. Most of the stop-go is pivots near obstacles flickering
# round the turn floor; 3-tick bursts make those longer, steadier turns.
# Back to the old drive: MODE_QUIET_MOTORS="0".
# 2026-10-10 (Harsh: "the 4 september one was best ... i just wanted add return
# to home ... you slowed the speed and now its bumping not energetic and also
# the steering and reaction speed"): ALL FOUR 10-04 smoothing layers OFF, the
# 09-04 drive back. Exploring phase from the run logs: 09-04 21:18 forward 27%
# of ticks at 0.25 m/s (max 0.50), stopped 22%; 10-10 01:07 forward 11% at
# 0.14 (max 0.38), stopped 51%; 13:45 forward 6%, stopped 62% -- and its bump
# was a COMMITTED pivot into a chair leg (ToF 0.40 -> 0.02), its hum the quiet
# drive's kick-less reverse at duty 81. Smooth again: set these back to 1 / 2 / 1.0.
MODE_QUIET_MOTORS="0"
# 2026-10-04, the same complaint, the next layer: near an obstacle forward is
# cut and she TURNS IN PLACE -- and the creep pulse chopped that turn into
# on/off stabs at the pivot floor. Steady turns (rl/pi_deploy.py steady_pivots):
# replayed on top of the quiet drive, test #5 stop<->move switches 60 -> 46 a
# minute, starts 74 -> 57, one-tick jolts 10 -> 6 (old drive: 71, 87, 43).
# What is left is the exploring's own stop/go between ticks (not the driver).
MODE_STEADY_TURNS="0"
# ...and the layer above the driver (Harsh, "DO whats still left"): blocked, the
# POLICY flipped its turn +1.6 <-> -1.6 rad/s 10-38 times a minute (35-45% back
# within a second), each flip a one-tick stop at the slew limiter. A turn taken
# while blocked is kept 1 s (pi_deploy._commit_turn: direction only, never
# through a stop, deliberate turns exempt), and a start from standstill waits
# for a second tick of "go" (stops never wait). Replayed on the 15:43 run with
# everything: switches 144 -> 116 a minute, starts 128 -> 103, one-tick jolts
# 56 -> 8, clunks 39 -> 0 (old drive -> all layers). Off: delete these two.
# MODE_START_DEBOUNCE="2"     # off 2026-10-10 (see above)
# MODE_TURN_COMMIT="1.0"      # off 2026-10-10 (see above)
# 2026-10-02 23:22 (test #5): with unstick OFF the 09-27 triple lock came back
# -- bumper 11 cm froze forward AND turning, the rear gate refused 304 reverses,
# and she sat at (0, 0) for ~60 s saying "Initiating recovery". The undo is the
# only thing that breaks it, so unstick is ON again, in KEEP-TRYING form: no
# "please move me" and no waiting for a person (what Harsh rejected).
MODE_UNSTICK="1"
MODE_UNSTICK_KEEP_TRYING="1"
